WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.265 --> 00:00:06.309
<i>In the criminal justice system.</i>

2
00:00:06.310 --> 00:00:07.658
<i>the people are represented</i>

3
00:00:07.659 --> 00:00:10.139
<i>by two separate. yet
equally important groups:</i>

4
00:00:10.140 --> 00:00:11.967
<i>the police. who
investigate crime.</i>

5
00:00:11.968 --> 00:00:14.883
<i>and the district attorneys.
who prosecute the offenders.</i>

6
00:00:14.884 --> 00:00:16.581
<i>These are their stories.</i>

7
00:00:18.496 --> 00:00:23.631
It's a great opportunity. but
these kids are like family.

8
00:00:23.632 --> 00:00:25.328
I believe in loyalty.

9
00:00:25.329 --> 00:00:27.722
I wish I didn't. I swear to God.

10
00:00:27.723 --> 00:00:29.985
Life would be easier.

11
00:00:29.986 --> 00:00:31.639
But this is my life.

12
00:00:31.640 --> 00:00:34.511
You don't get many
opportunities like this.

13
00:00:34.512 --> 00:00:37.602
- [whistles]
- Hey. I gotta go.

14
00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:43.042
Yeah.

15
00:00:43.043 --> 00:00:45.175
Thanks for listening.

16
00:00:52.922 --> 00:00:55.880
<i>[low suspenseful music]</i>

17
00:00:55.881 --> 00:00:59.884
<i>♪</i>

18
00:00:59.885 --> 00:01:01.712
Two shots to the chest.

19
00:01:01.713 --> 00:01:04.846
Guy over there said he heard
gunshots and called 911.

20
00:01:04.847 --> 00:01:07.109
Didn't see the shooter. though.

21
00:01:07.110 --> 00:01:09.198
Wallet and phone weren't
found on his person.

22
00:01:09.199 --> 00:01:12.071
But it's Nick Walsh.

23
00:01:12.072 --> 00:01:13.246
The coach?

24
00:01:13.247 --> 00:01:14.986
That's him.

25
00:01:14.987 --> 00:01:17.293
Big fan.

26
00:01:17.294 --> 00:01:20.383
Not easy to go back-to-back
in college basketball.

27
00:01:20.384 --> 00:01:22.124
Kentucky just offered this guy

28
00:01:22.125 --> 00:01:24.735
100 mil for five years.

29
00:01:24.736 --> 00:01:28.739
One more data point
that life ain't fair.

30
00:01:28.740 --> 00:01:31.133
Perp snatched his watch.

31
00:01:31.134 --> 00:01:33.744
Snatched a lot more than that.

32
00:01:33.745 --> 00:01:37.226
<i>[tense music]</i>

33
00:01:37.227 --> 00:01:40.229
<i>[dramatic music]</i>

34
00:01:40.230 --> 00:01:47.411
<i>♪</i>

35
00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:55.074
Watch Online Movies and Series for FREE
www.osdb.link/lm

36
00:02:23.578 --> 00:02:26.797
All right. Thanks
for your help.

37
00:02:26.798 --> 00:02:29.278
So the question is.
what was a big-time

38
00:02:29.279 --> 00:02:30.845
college coach doing
down here anyway?

39
00:02:30.846 --> 00:02:32.716
Can someone tell me how in 2024

40
00:02:32.717 --> 00:02:34.849
there's not a single camera
on one of these buildings?

41
00:02:34.850 --> 00:02:36.590
[phone ringing]

42
00:02:36.591 --> 00:02:39.854
Riley.

43
00:02:39.855 --> 00:02:41.595
Yeah. I'll be there in five.

44
00:02:41.596 --> 00:02:42.857
Hey. man. I got
a personal thing.

45
00:02:42.858 --> 00:02:44.860
I'll be back.

46
00:02:48.733 --> 00:02:50.430
<i>I really appreciate
the call. Ray.</i>

47
00:02:50.431 --> 00:02:52.736
Of course. I wish
I knew beforehand.

48
00:02:52.737 --> 00:02:55.871
Yeah. me too. but here we are.

49
00:03:01.268 --> 00:03:04.226
[sighs] Unbelievable.

50
00:03:04.227 --> 00:03:06.054
[chuckles] Vinny.
how you doing. man?

51
00:03:06.055 --> 00:03:08.274
Hey. they set me up.
- Mm.

52
00:03:08.275 --> 00:03:09.666
What do you call
that. entrapment?

53
00:03:09.667 --> 00:03:11.320
- Oh. you're a lawyer now. huh?
- Come on. man.

54
00:03:11.321 --> 00:03:12.713
I didn't have a
choice. all right?

55
00:03:12.714 --> 00:03:15.150
I need the money.
- Oh. you didn't have a choice.

56
00:03:15.151 --> 00:03:16.499
You didn't have a
choice but to sell guns.

57
00:03:16.500 --> 00:03:17.848
Is that what you're
saying to me?

58
00:03:17.849 --> 00:03:19.807
All right. I hear you.
All right. I messed up.

59
00:03:19.808 --> 00:03:22.244
You're right.

60
00:03:22.245 --> 00:03:24.378
Thanks for coming
down. I appreciate it.

61
00:03:28.860 --> 00:03:30.948
Good to see you too.

62
00:03:30.949 --> 00:03:32.341
<i>My partner and I
have been working</i>

63
00:03:32.342 --> 00:03:34.343
that neighborhood
for a few weeks.

64
00:03:34.344 --> 00:03:36.563
putting out word we
were looking for guns.

65
00:03:36.564 --> 00:03:39.043
- Yeah. and then what?
- Matt texted me.

66
00:03:39.044 --> 00:03:41.611
Said he had two heaters
he was trying to move.

67
00:03:41.612 --> 00:03:43.744
So we met up earlier today.

68
00:03:43.745 --> 00:03:46.921
I gave him two grand.
He gave me two guns.

69
00:03:46.922 --> 00:03:49.576
And we busted him.

70
00:03:49.577 --> 00:03:52.883
The guy can't get
out of his own way.

71
00:03:52.884 --> 00:03:54.145
[sighs]

72
00:03:54.146 --> 00:03:55.843
But he's my brother.
and I love him. so...

73
00:03:55.844 --> 00:03:57.236
I get it. Vince.

74
00:03:57.237 --> 00:03:59.281
but we're talking
about guns here.

75
00:03:59.282 --> 00:04:01.501
Hard to make a case
like this disappear.

76
00:04:01.502 --> 00:04:03.416
I understand.

77
00:04:03.417 --> 00:04:07.289
Listen. Matt runs with
a colorful crowd...

78
00:04:07.290 --> 00:04:10.771
hustlers. some real criminals.

79
00:04:10.772 --> 00:04:13.383
Maybe he can work it
off as an informant.

80
00:04:15.385 --> 00:04:17.430
Let me run it up the flagpole.

81
00:04:17.431 --> 00:04:19.259
I owe you one. Ray.

82
00:04:21.217 --> 00:04:23.697
Selling guns. That is no joke.

83
00:04:23.698 --> 00:04:26.569
What was he thinking?
- Man. I... [sighs]

84
00:04:26.570 --> 00:04:29.311
I don't even know
where to begin.

85
00:04:29.312 --> 00:04:31.487
You don't have to.
It's not your job.

86
00:04:31.488 --> 00:04:33.055
You're not your
brother's keeper.

87
00:04:34.839 --> 00:04:38.320
Yeah. sometimes I'm
not so sure about that.

88
00:04:38.321 --> 00:04:40.017
But he's a good guy...

89
00:04:40.018 --> 00:04:42.759
sometimes.
- A good guy who sells guns.

90
00:04:42.760 --> 00:04:46.981
95% of the time he's
all right. you know?

91
00:04:46.982 --> 00:04:49.766
Like when our dad got
sick. he stepped up.

92
00:04:49.767 --> 00:04:52.595
He took care of him.
no questions asked.

93
00:04:52.596 --> 00:04:55.990
Wasn't looking for a
medal. He just did it.

94
00:04:55.991 --> 00:04:58.775
It's the other 5% with Matt.

95
00:04:58.776 --> 00:05:01.082
And he just has a way
of finding trouble. man.

96
00:05:01.083 --> 00:05:04.694
He just digs himself
into hole after hole.

97
00:05:04.695 --> 00:05:07.698
and I am always the one
that has to dig him out.

98
00:05:11.659 --> 00:05:14.791
Mrs. Walsh. I know
how difficult this is.

99
00:05:14.792 --> 00:05:18.708
and I am very sorry
for your loss.

100
00:05:18.709 --> 00:05:21.189
You mentioned that you had
just spoken to your husband.

101
00:05:21.190 --> 00:05:22.887
Do you know what time that was?

102
00:05:24.367 --> 00:05:25.672
Around 4:00.

103
00:05:25.673 --> 00:05:27.543
Do you know where he was?

104
00:05:27.544 --> 00:05:29.371
Who he might have been with?

105
00:05:29.372 --> 00:05:31.634
No.

106
00:05:31.635 --> 00:05:34.594
We were talking about
whether to stay or go.

107
00:05:34.595 --> 00:05:37.466
Kentucky made a
really generous offer.

108
00:05:37.467 --> 00:05:40.034
more than double what
we're making now. but...

109
00:05:40.035 --> 00:05:43.385
but Nick really loved Hudson

110
00:05:43.386 --> 00:05:46.823
and his coaches and his players.

111
00:05:46.824 --> 00:05:49.260
He's just so damn principled.

112
00:05:49.261 --> 00:05:51.916
It was making
everything really hard.

113
00:05:53.788 --> 00:05:58.922
Ma'am. did your husband wear
a watch on his left wrist?

114
00:05:58.923 --> 00:06:00.924
Can you describe it?

115
00:06:00.925 --> 00:06:07.278
It's a Rolex with a platinum
and gold band and a blue face.

116
00:06:07.279 --> 00:06:09.019
Any inscriptions on it?

117
00:06:09.020 --> 00:06:11.326
No.

118
00:06:11.327 --> 00:06:12.849
Why?

119
00:06:12.850 --> 00:06:14.982
The watch was
missing. so we're just

120
00:06:14.983 --> 00:06:16.593
collecting information
at this point.

121
00:06:18.073 --> 00:06:20.902
Was anyone harassing or
threatening your husband?

122
00:06:22.730 --> 00:06:25.862
Not that I'm aware
of. [sniffles]

123
00:06:25.863 --> 00:06:28.517
But the past few
weeks have been crazy.

124
00:06:28.518 --> 00:06:33.043
It felt like the whole city was
threatening and harassing us.

125
00:06:33.044 --> 00:06:36.090
People would walk up
to us in a restaurant.

126
00:06:36.091 --> 00:06:38.005
You can't leave us. Coach.

127
00:06:38.006 --> 00:06:41.923
My whole world revolves
around Hudson basketball.

128
00:06:44.926 --> 00:06:47.231
Actually. I saw him
arguing with someone

129
00:06:47.232 --> 00:06:48.711
outside of our building.

130
00:06:48.712 --> 00:06:50.452
<i>[suspenseful music]</i>

131
00:06:50.453 --> 00:06:53.803
- When was this?
- Two days ago.

132
00:06:53.804 --> 00:06:56.023
So the wife was home
most of the day.

133
00:06:56.024 --> 00:06:57.894
By all appearances. they
had a great relationship.

134
00:06:57.895 --> 00:07:00.157
They met in college.
got married at 24.

135
00:07:00.158 --> 00:07:02.333
- American dream.
- Something like that.

136
00:07:02.334 --> 00:07:03.900
Yo!

137
00:07:03.901 --> 00:07:06.250
Hey. I found a video of
Walsh arguing with somebody.

138
00:07:06.251 --> 00:07:08.296
Check this out.

139
00:07:08.297 --> 00:07:10.646
Can you zoom in
on the other guy?

140
00:07:10.647 --> 00:07:12.431
That's the best I can do.

141
00:07:12.432 --> 00:07:14.433
Wait. Freeze it there.

142
00:07:14.434 --> 00:07:16.217
- Mm-hmm.
- It's a badge.

143
00:07:16.218 --> 00:07:18.915
And it's not NYPD.

144
00:07:18.916 --> 00:07:21.440
Walsh was arguing
with an FBI agent.

145
00:07:21.441 --> 00:07:24.618
<i>♪</i>

146
00:07:28.491 --> 00:07:30.492
I met with Walsh three days ago.

147
00:07:30.493 --> 00:07:31.580
Looked more like
an argument to me.

148
00:07:31.581 --> 00:07:32.929
Yeah. he ran hot.

149
00:07:32.930 --> 00:07:34.496
Lots of emotion.

150
00:07:34.497 --> 00:07:36.585
Was this conversation
personal or professional?

151
00:07:36.586 --> 00:07:38.152
Professional.

152
00:07:38.153 --> 00:07:39.501
Some rich alumnus threatened
to destroy his life.

153
00:07:39.502 --> 00:07:40.850
Why?

154
00:07:40.851 --> 00:07:42.069
Because he was thinking
about leaving Hudson?

155
00:07:42.070 --> 00:07:43.549
Crazy. right?

156
00:07:43.550 --> 00:07:45.638
But these boosters take
this stuff very seriously.

157
00:07:45.639 --> 00:07:49.424
And according to Walsh.
this guy had the resources

158
00:07:49.425 --> 00:07:51.296
and the conviction
to pull it off.

159
00:07:53.211 --> 00:07:54.951
He got nervous.

160
00:07:54.952 --> 00:07:57.345
Called an agent down in
Atlanta... his cousin. I think.

161
00:07:57.346 --> 00:07:59.303
She asked if I could help out.

162
00:07:59.304 --> 00:08:00.957
Why was Walsh so mad?

163
00:08:00.958 --> 00:08:02.742
He changed his mind.

164
00:08:02.743 --> 00:08:05.179
He said he didn't wanna get
this booster in trouble.

165
00:08:05.180 --> 00:08:07.442
Said he overreacted.

166
00:08:07.443 --> 00:08:09.357
When I made it clear that
it wasn't that easy...

167
00:08:09.358 --> 00:08:11.054
genie's out of the bottle...

168
00:08:11.055 --> 00:08:13.622
he got upset.
- Hmm.

169
00:08:13.623 --> 00:08:15.495
This booster got a name?

170
00:08:17.758 --> 00:08:20.194
I just wrote that
stubborn Irish prick

171
00:08:20.195 --> 00:08:21.543
a check for $2 million.

172
00:08:21.544 --> 00:08:23.545
and he's thinking of
walking out on me.

173
00:08:23.546 --> 00:08:25.939
heading to Kentucky?
- Wait. hold on.

174
00:08:25.940 --> 00:08:27.723
You wrote a check
for 2 mil for what?

175
00:08:27.724 --> 00:08:30.247
A 6'7" point guard from LA

176
00:08:30.248 --> 00:08:32.380
who plays defense
like Gary Payton

177
00:08:32.381 --> 00:08:34.382
and shoots like Ray Allen.

178
00:08:34.383 --> 00:08:36.297
Number one recruit
in the country.

179
00:08:36.298 --> 00:08:38.212
Kid's agent wanted 3 mil.

180
00:08:38.213 --> 00:08:41.128
I was able to get it done
for 2 with a 500.000 kicker

181
00:08:41.129 --> 00:08:42.564
if we win the championship.

182
00:08:42.565 --> 00:08:44.697
All this money to play
college basketball now.

183
00:08:44.698 --> 00:08:47.264
Yeah. no rules anymore.
It's the Wild West.

184
00:08:47.265 --> 00:08:49.789
It's really fun.
- Oh. it's fun.

185
00:08:49.790 --> 00:08:52.661
Like getting shot in the chest
in a vacant lot kind of fun?

186
00:08:52.662 --> 00:08:53.967
Yeah. that's...

187
00:08:53.968 --> 00:08:55.882
I can't believe
he's really gone.

188
00:08:55.883 --> 00:08:58.711
I've been crying like a
baby ever since I found out.

189
00:08:58.712 --> 00:09:00.451
You've been crying like a
baby since he's been gone.

190
00:09:00.452 --> 00:09:02.105
and you've been threatening
to ruin his life?

191
00:09:02.106 --> 00:09:03.454
Correct.

192
00:09:03.455 --> 00:09:05.631
The threat had to
do with business.

193
00:09:05.632 --> 00:09:07.154
I pledged 10 million

194
00:09:07.155 --> 00:09:08.851
for a new practice
facility this year.

195
00:09:08.852 --> 00:09:11.158
That's on top of the 2
million for the kid from LA

196
00:09:11.159 --> 00:09:13.334
So I'm long 12 mil
just this year.

197
00:09:13.335 --> 00:09:14.683
And he's gonna walk out on me?

198
00:09:14.684 --> 00:09:18.426
Hell. no. But as a
person. I loved him.

199
00:09:18.427 --> 00:09:20.471
I mean. where I'm from.
you don't try to destroy

200
00:09:20.472 --> 00:09:23.257
the people you love. but...
- I threatened to destroy him.

201
00:09:23.258 --> 00:09:24.780
I was just negotiating.

202
00:09:24.781 --> 00:09:27.522
Look. I wanted to scare
him. to keep him in Hudson.

203
00:09:27.523 --> 00:09:30.264
Where were you the day of
the murder at 4:30 p.m.?

204
00:09:30.265 --> 00:09:34.050
In a meeting here
with 20 people.

205
00:09:34.051 --> 00:09:36.923
Look. I didn't kill Coach Walsh.

206
00:09:36.924 --> 00:09:39.534
Any idea what he was doing
on the Lower East Side?

207
00:09:39.535 --> 00:09:40.579
No.

208
00:09:40.580 --> 00:09:42.189
Any of his friends live there?

209
00:09:42.190 --> 00:09:43.494
Not that I know of.

210
00:09:43.495 --> 00:09:45.192
One of his players does. though.

211
00:09:45.193 --> 00:09:48.325
Well. former player. actually.

212
00:09:48.326 --> 00:09:51.459
Coach cut him from the
team three days ago.

213
00:09:51.460 --> 00:09:53.243
The kid get upset about that?

214
00:09:53.244 --> 00:09:54.636
I'm not sure. His
father was. though.

215
00:09:54.637 --> 00:09:56.638
He went crazy.

216
00:09:56.639 --> 00:09:58.335
I can't say I blame him. either.

217
00:09:58.336 --> 00:09:59.859
Cost the kid a million bucks.

218
00:09:59.860 --> 00:10:02.296
You think the father
is capable of violence?

219
00:10:02.297 --> 00:10:04.559
For a million dollars?

220
00:10:04.560 --> 00:10:06.605
Anyone is.

221
00:10:06.606 --> 00:10:09.608
<i>[tense music]</i>

222
00:10:09.609 --> 00:10:11.392
<i>♪</i>

223
00:10:11.393 --> 00:10:15.004
We hung out for about an hour.

224
00:10:15.005 --> 00:10:16.527
Was that typical?

225
00:10:16.528 --> 00:10:18.007
Was there any reason
Coach was there?

226
00:10:18.008 --> 00:10:21.228
I guess he felt bad and
wanted to make it right.

227
00:10:21.229 --> 00:10:23.360
If you ask me.
that son of a bitch

228
00:10:23.361 --> 00:10:26.320
needed to make it right.
- Yeah. I get it.

229
00:10:26.321 --> 00:10:28.583
Cost Malik a lot of
money. You too. huh?

230
00:10:28.584 --> 00:10:30.411
$1 million.

231
00:10:30.412 --> 00:10:33.719
And he just... he didn't care.

232
00:10:33.720 --> 00:10:35.851
Told Malik to go home.

233
00:10:35.852 --> 00:10:38.245
He had no right to do that.

234
00:10:38.246 --> 00:10:40.682
You feel the same
way about that?

235
00:10:40.683 --> 00:10:42.379
I mean. I was...

236
00:10:42.380 --> 00:10:44.643
I was upset. but...

237
00:10:44.644 --> 00:10:47.733
- What?
- It was my fault.

238
00:10:47.734 --> 00:10:50.997
I wasn't as focused
as I should have been.

239
00:10:50.998 --> 00:10:52.912
I was late to practice a lot.

240
00:10:52.913 --> 00:10:55.566
I was focusing on things
other than basketball.

241
00:10:55.567 --> 00:10:58.874
you know. getting endorsements.
doing TikToks. rapping.

242
00:10:58.875 --> 00:11:01.748
So I get it.

243
00:11:03.663 --> 00:11:05.925
What time did Coach
leave the house?

244
00:11:05.926 --> 00:11:07.448
Around 4:00.

245
00:11:07.449 --> 00:11:09.624
And that's the last
time you guys saw him.

246
00:11:09.625 --> 00:11:10.886
Yes. sir.

247
00:11:10.887 --> 00:11:14.063
Did Walsh say anything
about where he was going

248
00:11:14.064 --> 00:11:16.371
or if he was meeting anybody?

249
00:11:20.767 --> 00:11:24.334
Coach came in
around 4:15 or so.

250
00:11:24.335 --> 00:11:26.293
He was here for
about 20 minutes.

251
00:11:26.294 --> 00:11:28.469
You happen to see who
he was talking to?

252
00:11:28.470 --> 00:11:30.166
I'm pretty sure he was alone...

253
00:11:30.167 --> 00:11:32.038
most of the time. anyway.

254
00:11:32.039 --> 00:11:34.083
But I gotta be honest.

255
00:11:34.084 --> 00:11:36.477
I wasn't really
paying attention.

256
00:11:36.478 --> 00:11:39.132
Was he alone when he left?

257
00:11:39.133 --> 00:11:41.656
Uh. sorry. I didn't notice.

258
00:11:41.657 --> 00:11:43.789
How about was anybody
bothering or harassing him?

259
00:11:43.790 --> 00:11:44.877
Nah.

260
00:11:44.878 --> 00:11:46.705
People here mind
their own business.

261
00:11:46.706 --> 00:11:49.664
Do you mind if we take a look
at your surveillance video?

262
00:11:49.665 --> 00:11:51.840
Don't have any.

263
00:11:51.841 --> 00:11:53.624
Nothing?

264
00:11:53.625 --> 00:11:55.945
Like I said. people here tend
to mind their own business.

265
00:11:58.587 --> 00:12:00.806
All right. Thank you.

266
00:12:00.807 --> 00:12:02.416
Learn anything new?

267
00:12:02.417 --> 00:12:03.896
Yeah. that. apparently.
college basketball is

268
00:12:03.897 --> 00:12:05.724
now professional basketball.

269
00:12:05.725 --> 00:12:07.987
These kids are literally
making millions of dollars.

270
00:12:07.988 --> 00:12:11.468
Yeah. NIL changed everything.

271
00:12:11.469 --> 00:12:15.298
I grew up going to St.
John's games with my dad.

272
00:12:15.299 --> 00:12:16.691
Well. we're getting
closer at least.

273
00:12:16.692 --> 00:12:18.345
Looks like the last
place Walsh was seen

274
00:12:18.346 --> 00:12:19.912
was at Clancy's.
the bar a few blocks

275
00:12:19.913 --> 00:12:21.827
down the street from the
vacant lot where he was shot.

276
00:12:21.828 --> 00:12:24.046
We're actually closer
than you think we are.

277
00:12:24.047 --> 00:12:27.049
Just found video of Walsh
from the hardware store

278
00:12:27.050 --> 00:12:29.269
across the street from Clancy's.

279
00:12:29.270 --> 00:12:31.924
And there he is. leaving
the bar at 4:34 p.m..

280
00:12:31.925 --> 00:12:33.229
and he's with another guy.

281
00:12:33.230 --> 00:12:34.578
Music to my ears.

282
00:12:34.579 --> 00:12:36.450
Clean angle too.
How about that?

283
00:12:36.451 --> 00:12:38.495
Run it through facial rec.

284
00:12:38.496 --> 00:12:40.280
<i>[suspenseful music]</i>

285
00:12:40.281 --> 00:12:42.412
No need.

286
00:12:42.413 --> 00:12:44.327
It's my brother.

287
00:12:44.328 --> 00:12:50.421
<i>♪</i>

288
00:12:54.121 --> 00:12:55.686
I don't get it.

289
00:12:55.687 --> 00:12:57.384
What's everybody
so worked up about?

290
00:12:57.385 --> 00:12:58.820
Well. you see. Matty. we're
kind of investigating a murder.

291
00:12:58.821 --> 00:13:00.082
You might have been
the last person seen

292
00:13:00.083 --> 00:13:02.171
with the dead guy prior
to him being dead.

293
00:13:02.172 --> 00:13:03.825
So you and Walsh left
the bar together.

294
00:13:03.826 --> 00:13:05.218
Why is that?

295
00:13:05.219 --> 00:13:06.959
Guys. I hope you know
I had nothing to do

296
00:13:06.960 --> 00:13:08.743
with Walsh's death.
You know that. right?

297
00:13:08.744 --> 00:13:09.700
Will you just
answer the question

298
00:13:09.701 --> 00:13:12.094
for once in your life. please?

299
00:13:12.095 --> 00:13:13.922
I was having a beer at Clancy's.

300
00:13:13.923 --> 00:13:15.184
I saw the guy
heading for the door.

301
00:13:15.185 --> 00:13:17.404
I figured I'd walk
over and say hi.

302
00:13:17.405 --> 00:13:19.449
You know. we played against
each other in high school.

303
00:13:19.450 --> 00:13:20.711
I had 17 points.

304
00:13:20.712 --> 00:13:21.843
Fantastic.

305
00:13:21.844 --> 00:13:24.019
Yeah. he remembered
me. No lie.

306
00:13:24.020 --> 00:13:25.194
Said I had one of the prettiest

307
00:13:25.195 --> 00:13:26.717
left-handed jump
shots he'd ever seen.

308
00:13:26.718 --> 00:13:28.328
That's great. Matt. but we're
a little more interested

309
00:13:28.329 --> 00:13:30.460
in the murder than your
jump shot right now. okay?

310
00:13:30.461 --> 00:13:32.462
What'd you guys do
when you left the bar?

311
00:13:32.463 --> 00:13:35.030
Walked for a few blocks
down by the bridge.

312
00:13:35.031 --> 00:13:36.118
I asked if he was gonna
take that Kentucky job.

313
00:13:36.119 --> 00:13:37.641
He didn't really answer me.

314
00:13:37.642 --> 00:13:40.383
Said he was thinking about
it. but that he loved Hudson.

315
00:13:40.384 --> 00:13:42.864
- Okay. then what?
- And then nothing.

316
00:13:42.865 --> 00:13:43.909
He got a phone call.
and he walked away.

317
00:13:43.910 --> 00:13:45.388
That was it.

318
00:13:45.389 --> 00:13:46.955
Was anybody watching
him or waiting for him?

319
00:13:46.956 --> 00:13:48.739
No. not really.

320
00:13:48.740 --> 00:13:52.134
I mean. other than Jackie.

321
00:13:52.135 --> 00:13:54.006
You gonna tell us who Jackie is?

322
00:13:54.007 --> 00:13:55.877
Jackie Costa. He
owns Clancy's.

323
00:13:55.878 --> 00:13:58.837
And what was Jackie Costa doing?

324
00:13:58.838 --> 00:14:01.143
Standing on a box
smoking a cigarette.

325
00:14:01.144 --> 00:14:03.363
Okay. so you and
Walsh part ways.

326
00:14:03.364 --> 00:14:05.321
and Costa is just standing
there smoking a cigarette.

327
00:14:05.322 --> 00:14:06.714
That's it?

328
00:14:06.715 --> 00:14:08.804
Does anybody have a lighter?

329
00:14:10.588 --> 00:14:14.591
Like I said before. I was
here all afternoon working.

330
00:14:14.592 --> 00:14:16.071
Step outside for a few?

331
00:14:16.072 --> 00:14:18.421
Maybe take a walk?
- No.

332
00:14:18.422 --> 00:14:20.032
Maybe take a little smoke break?

333
00:14:20.033 --> 00:14:21.511
I gave it up.

334
00:14:21.512 --> 00:14:23.296
I heard a rumor it was
bad for your health.

335
00:14:23.297 --> 00:14:26.125
- [chuckles]
- Yeah. I heard that one too.

336
00:14:26.126 --> 00:14:27.822
Why are you guys asking
all these questions?

337
00:14:27.823 --> 00:14:29.998
I already told you what
I saw. what I know.

338
00:14:29.999 --> 00:14:31.565
Yeah. yeah.

339
00:14:31.566 --> 00:14:33.872
Well. we talked to someone
who said that they saw Walsh

340
00:14:33.873 --> 00:14:35.047
walking down Sixth
Street. and they thought

341
00:14:35.048 --> 00:14:36.787
that they maybe saw you too.

342
00:14:36.788 --> 00:14:37.919
So. you know. we're
just following up.

343
00:14:37.920 --> 00:14:39.094
He's wrong.

344
00:14:39.095 --> 00:14:41.444
I was inside the
bar all afternoon.

345
00:14:41.445 --> 00:14:43.098
Got it.

346
00:14:43.099 --> 00:14:45.145
- Thanks for your time.
- Mm-hmm.

347
00:14:47.974 --> 00:14:51.628
He's lying his ass off.
about the smoking anyway.

348
00:14:51.629 --> 00:14:54.936
Had a pack of cigarettes
in his jacket pocket.

349
00:14:54.937 --> 00:14:57.243
So Costa's alibi checks out.

350
00:14:57.244 --> 00:14:59.288
Talked to the dishwasher.
the bartender.

351
00:14:59.289 --> 00:15:02.813
two guys who claimed to be
at the bar from 3:00 to 6:00.

352
00:15:02.814 --> 00:15:06.817
and everybody says that Costa
was at the bar the entire time.

353
00:15:06.818 --> 00:15:09.037
and they said he quit smoking.

354
00:15:09.038 --> 00:15:10.734
and they were
adamant about that.

355
00:15:10.735 --> 00:15:12.562
Yeah. those guys would
say he played shortstop

356
00:15:12.563 --> 00:15:14.129
for the Yankees if
he asked them to.

357
00:15:14.130 --> 00:15:15.826
- Mm-hmm.
- Costa is no joke.

358
00:15:15.827 --> 00:15:17.263
I pulled his sheet.

359
00:15:17.264 --> 00:15:19.047
He's got priors for
racketeering. gambling.

360
00:15:19.048 --> 00:15:20.744
assault. and narcotics.

361
00:15:20.745 --> 00:15:22.659
- Oh. busy boy. huh?
- Yeah.

362
00:15:22.660 --> 00:15:24.748
And as suspected. he's a liar.

363
00:15:24.749 --> 00:15:27.490
I found video of him two
blocks from the crime scene

364
00:15:27.491 --> 00:15:30.058
three minutes after
the 911 call at 4:43.

365
00:15:30.059 --> 00:15:32.626
So Costa was not
inside the bar all day.

366
00:15:32.627 --> 00:15:34.889
no matter what his friends say.
- I like him for it.

367
00:15:34.890 --> 00:15:36.586
Yeah. we just gotta
find a way to put him

368
00:15:36.587 --> 00:15:38.501
and Walsh together
prior to the murder.

369
00:15:38.502 --> 00:15:40.851
- Mm-hmm.
- Can you pull more video?

370
00:15:40.852 --> 00:15:44.029
It's pretty thin down
there. Not a lot of cameras.

371
00:15:44.030 --> 00:15:45.813
All right. well.
just... I don't know...

372
00:15:45.814 --> 00:15:48.511
keep pressing the friends.
I mean. you never know.

373
00:15:48.512 --> 00:15:51.166
We can try. but that code
of silence thing is real.

374
00:15:51.167 --> 00:15:52.515
These guys are not gonna budge.

375
00:15:52.516 --> 00:15:55.127
It's how they define
themselves. you know?

376
00:15:55.128 --> 00:15:57.999
Maybe we come at this
from a different angle.

377
00:15:58.000 --> 00:16:00.915
Maybe we try to get
Costa to talk instead.

378
00:16:00.916 --> 00:16:03.831
<i>[tense music]</i>

379
00:16:03.832 --> 00:16:06.007
So what's going on?

380
00:16:06.008 --> 00:16:08.009
This morning. I'm
making an omelet.

381
00:16:08.010 --> 00:16:09.793
You know. avocado.
sausage. peppers. all that.

382
00:16:09.794 --> 00:16:11.795
Doorbell rings. and I'm
thinking it's Amazon.

383
00:16:11.796 --> 00:16:13.841
or maybe it's the lady next
door with the dementia.

384
00:16:13.842 --> 00:16:15.974
or it's...
- For God's sake. Matty.

385
00:16:15.975 --> 00:16:18.454
Yeah. sorry. I get
a little rattled.

386
00:16:18.455 --> 00:16:22.328
I go to the door. and
it's two cops. detectives.

387
00:16:22.329 --> 00:16:24.461
They start asking about Walsh.

388
00:16:26.986 --> 00:16:28.725
What's that got to do with me?

389
00:16:28.726 --> 00:16:30.640
They think you're involved.

390
00:16:30.641 --> 00:16:32.512
<i>Excuse me?</i>

391
00:16:32.513 --> 00:16:35.689
<i>They. uh. kept asking
questions about you.</i>

392
00:16:35.690 --> 00:16:38.387
<i>So that's why you're here?</i>

393
00:16:38.388 --> 00:16:41.651
<i>To find out if what?
If I was involved?</i>

394
00:16:41.652 --> 00:16:43.784
- He's getting suspicious.
- No. he's okay.

395
00:16:43.785 --> 00:16:45.438
Matty can handle this.

396
00:16:45.439 --> 00:16:46.439
Jackie. please.

397
00:16:46.440 --> 00:16:47.962
I'm just trying to help you out.

398
00:16:47.963 --> 00:16:50.356
I mean. I figured it
was best if I came

399
00:16:50.357 --> 00:16:52.010
and just told you what
happened. you know?

400
00:16:52.011 --> 00:16:55.404
- What kind of questions?
- You know. if I...

401
00:16:55.405 --> 00:16:57.406
if I saw you leave
the bar together.

402
00:16:57.407 --> 00:17:02.281
if I saw you and Walsh talking.
if you guys had any bad blood.

403
00:17:02.282 --> 00:17:04.761
I appreciate you
giving me the heads up.

404
00:17:04.762 --> 00:17:08.939
Yeah. yeah. like I said.
I'm just here to help.

405
00:17:08.940 --> 00:17:10.767
Hey. look. I know
you're a good guy.

406
00:17:10.768 --> 00:17:12.943
but I gotta be honest.

407
00:17:12.944 --> 00:17:15.120
You're making me nervous.

408
00:17:15.121 --> 00:17:17.426
He's good. He's still good.

409
00:17:17.427 --> 00:17:21.126
So. what. you wanna
search me for a wire?

410
00:17:21.127 --> 00:17:23.128
It would make me feel better.

411
00:17:23.129 --> 00:17:30.265
<i>♪</i>

412
00:17:30.266 --> 00:17:35.270
I'm insulted. but.
hey. I get it.

413
00:17:35.271 --> 00:17:38.665
These are stressful
times. right?

414
00:17:38.666 --> 00:17:40.710
Go ahead.

415
00:17:40.711 --> 00:17:47.675
<i>♪</i>

416
00:17:54.247 --> 00:17:56.030
Okay. Sorry about that.

417
00:17:56.031 --> 00:17:57.206
You good? [chuckles]

418
00:18:01.906 --> 00:18:04.517
I appreciate you looking out.

419
00:18:04.518 --> 00:18:06.562
The truth is. I might
need some help with this

420
00:18:06.563 --> 00:18:08.303
down the road if these
guys keep sniffing.

421
00:18:08.304 --> 00:18:09.913
Of course. I'm happy to help.

422
00:18:09.914 --> 00:18:11.350
Good.

423
00:18:11.351 --> 00:18:14.004
So these cops happen to tell you

424
00:18:14.005 --> 00:18:16.137
if they had any evidence. video.

425
00:18:16.138 --> 00:18:18.052
witnesses. anything like that?

426
00:18:18.053 --> 00:18:21.360
No. they. uh. they didn't say.

427
00:18:21.361 --> 00:18:23.797
The funny thing is.
I didn't know Walsh.

428
00:18:23.798 --> 00:18:27.148
This former player of
his. this kid Crawford.

429
00:18:27.149 --> 00:18:29.324
he owed me 75 grand.

430
00:18:29.325 --> 00:18:31.153
Now we're cooking.
Now we're cooking.

431
00:18:33.677 --> 00:18:35.330
Whoa. whoa. whoa.
whoa. What happened?

432
00:18:35.331 --> 00:18:37.638
What happened? What
happened to the feed?

433
00:18:39.379 --> 00:18:40.683
- Hey. no. no.
- What did you do?

434
00:18:40.684 --> 00:18:42.163
- I don't know what happened.
- I got this.

435
00:18:42.164 --> 00:18:43.512
Where's the camera?
- I don't know.

436
00:18:43.513 --> 00:18:44.774
- Where's the button?
- I don't know.

437
00:18:44.775 --> 00:18:46.341
Maybe it fell off.

438
00:18:46.342 --> 00:18:47.777
Do not lie to us. Matt.
Do you understand?

439
00:18:47.778 --> 00:18:48.952
Do not lie. Just tell
us what happened.

440
00:18:48.953 --> 00:18:50.085
What happened was...

441
00:18:52.435 --> 00:18:54.523
What happened was I
realized I'm not a snitch.

442
00:18:54.524 --> 00:18:56.351
All right. look.
I'm not ratting out

443
00:18:56.352 --> 00:18:57.787
a friend of mine. a friend
who's been good to me.

444
00:18:57.788 --> 00:18:59.572
who's lent me money.
who's helped me find jobs.

445
00:18:59.573 --> 00:19:01.487
unlike some people. by the way.
- Oh. here we go.

446
00:19:01.488 --> 00:19:02.749
I'm just telling the
truth here. Vince.

447
00:19:02.750 --> 00:19:04.185
You can't even help
yourself. can you?

448
00:19:04.186 --> 00:19:05.317
You know what? I did
what I had to do.

449
00:19:05.318 --> 00:19:06.535
You know. I put my
name on the line.

450
00:19:06.536 --> 00:19:07.710
- Oh. yeah?
- Get out of my face.

451
00:19:07.711 --> 00:19:09.495
Hey. hey. hey. hey.
Watch yourself.

452
00:19:09.496 --> 00:19:11.149
Because I'm not your
brother. You feel me?

453
00:19:11.150 --> 00:19:12.367
You look me in
the eye right now.

454
00:19:12.368 --> 00:19:15.805
You tell me. did Costa
admit to the murder?

455
00:19:15.806 --> 00:19:17.460
Yes or no?

456
00:19:21.725 --> 00:19:23.857
You know what?

457
00:19:23.858 --> 00:19:25.554
We're done talking.

458
00:19:25.555 --> 00:19:31.518
<i>♪</i>

459
00:19:35.739 --> 00:19:38.959
What does that mean.
his wire malfunctioned?

460
00:19:38.960 --> 00:19:41.353
I mean. Matty got nervous. so...

461
00:19:41.354 --> 00:19:42.571
Why?

462
00:19:42.572 --> 00:19:44.094
Because he thought
Costa made him?

463
00:19:44.095 --> 00:19:46.140
I guess so.

464
00:19:46.141 --> 00:19:48.229
Look. we still got
some good information.

465
00:19:48.230 --> 00:19:50.840
Costa said that one of
Walsh's former players

466
00:19:50.841 --> 00:19:52.190
owed him a bunch of money.

467
00:19:52.191 --> 00:19:53.800
So we know that
there's a connection.

468
00:19:53.801 --> 00:19:56.063
So maybe Walsh was there
to smooth things over.

469
00:19:56.064 --> 00:19:59.327
you know. ask for leniency
for the kid or something.

470
00:19:59.328 --> 00:20:01.068
Okay. that's good.

471
00:20:01.069 --> 00:20:03.592
I'm still trying to understand

472
00:20:03.593 --> 00:20:06.900
what happened with
your brother's wire.

473
00:20:06.901 --> 00:20:09.207
- Like I said...
- I know what you said.

474
00:20:09.208 --> 00:20:11.165
But now I wanna
know what happened.

475
00:20:11.166 --> 00:20:14.299
<i>[tense music]</i>

476
00:20:14.300 --> 00:20:17.258
The button fell off.
and Matt stepped on it.

477
00:20:17.259 --> 00:20:19.347
To protect himself?

478
00:20:19.348 --> 00:20:20.435
That's what he said.

479
00:20:20.436 --> 00:20:22.612
And do you believe him?

480
00:20:25.224 --> 00:20:26.702
No.

481
00:20:26.703 --> 00:20:29.488
Okay. well. next time.
lead with the truth.

482
00:20:29.489 --> 00:20:31.230
and then we'll get along better.

483
00:20:34.407 --> 00:20:36.756
Got some good news.

484
00:20:36.757 --> 00:20:39.411
Tracked down the former
player. Crawford.

485
00:20:39.412 --> 00:20:41.762
Got a work address. Let's go.

486
00:20:44.591 --> 00:20:46.287
<i>Yeah. that's... that's true.</i>

487
00:20:46.288 --> 00:20:49.290
I owe Costa 75 grand.

488
00:20:49.291 --> 00:20:50.596
More than that. actually.

489
00:20:50.597 --> 00:20:51.945
because the interest
he's charging.

490
00:20:51.946 --> 00:20:53.599
Why do you owe him the money?

491
00:20:53.600 --> 00:20:55.165
I like to gamble.

492
00:20:55.166 --> 00:20:57.124
You know why Walsh was
going to meet him that day?

493
00:20:57.125 --> 00:20:58.995
Did it have something
to do with your debt?

494
00:20:58.996 --> 00:21:02.782
All right. I needed money.
so I reached out to Coach.

495
00:21:02.783 --> 00:21:04.305
and God bless him.

496
00:21:04.306 --> 00:21:06.829
He said he'd take care of
it. under one condition.

497
00:21:06.830 --> 00:21:10.442
that I get help
for my addiction.

498
00:21:10.443 --> 00:21:12.095
Why?

499
00:21:12.096 --> 00:21:14.446
Y'all don't think
Costa was involved?

500
00:21:14.447 --> 00:21:16.361
We don't know yet. We're
still investigating.

501
00:21:16.362 --> 00:21:19.625
So tell me. did
Coach actually say

502
00:21:19.626 --> 00:21:21.017
that he was gonna
meet with Costa?

503
00:21:21.018 --> 00:21:23.629
I told him where Costa worked.

504
00:21:23.630 --> 00:21:25.152
and Coach said he'd
take care of it.

505
00:21:25.153 --> 00:21:28.111
Now. that's all I know.
- He say when?

506
00:21:28.112 --> 00:21:30.462
No. he just said
that he'd handle it.

507
00:21:30.463 --> 00:21:31.811
Uh-huh.

508
00:21:31.812 --> 00:21:33.334
Look. this is on me. man.

509
00:21:33.335 --> 00:21:34.988
I should have never
gotten him involved.

510
00:21:34.989 --> 00:21:36.206
You know. I was
just a role player.

511
00:21:36.207 --> 00:21:38.339
scoring 3 points
a game. but he...

512
00:21:38.340 --> 00:21:42.213
Look. thanks for being
straight with us. all right?

513
00:21:44.215 --> 00:21:45.999
The dots are all
starting to connect.

514
00:21:46.000 --> 00:21:47.653
and they all lead back to Costa.

515
00:21:47.654 --> 00:21:50.482
Yeah. we're still not there
yet because of your brother.

516
00:21:50.483 --> 00:21:53.180
Had he not killed the
wire. we'd be done by now.

517
00:21:53.181 --> 00:21:55.051
Costa would be in Rikers
staring down murder two.

518
00:21:55.052 --> 00:21:56.662
Tell me I'm wrong.
- Yeah. man. I get it.

519
00:21:56.663 --> 00:21:57.837
But that's just
Matty. all right?

520
00:21:57.838 --> 00:21:59.665
It's just the way he is.
- What?

521
00:21:59.666 --> 00:22:01.536
Do you even hear
yourself right now?

522
00:22:01.537 --> 00:22:03.321
That's not an excuse.

523
00:22:03.322 --> 00:22:05.018
What. you have some biological
urge to cover for his dumb ass?

524
00:22:05.019 --> 00:22:06.802
Whoa. whoa. whoa.
Take it easy.

525
00:22:06.803 --> 00:22:08.369
He's still my brother.

526
00:22:08.370 --> 00:22:09.936
And what does that mean. Vince?

527
00:22:09.937 --> 00:22:11.851
You gotta protect him
until the day he dies?

528
00:22:11.852 --> 00:22:13.505
What do you want me to do?

529
00:22:13.506 --> 00:22:15.246
I'm supposed to sell him out?

530
00:22:19.468 --> 00:22:22.165
Let's just...

531
00:22:22.166 --> 00:22:25.038
okay. you're right
about one thing.

532
00:22:25.039 --> 00:22:26.996
Crawford's statement is helpful.

533
00:22:26.997 --> 00:22:30.565
It links Costa and
Walsh. sort of.

534
00:22:30.566 --> 00:22:32.001
It's good enough for a warrant.

535
00:22:32.002 --> 00:22:34.961
<i>[tense music]</i>

536
00:22:34.962 --> 00:22:37.398
<i>♪</i>

537
00:22:37.399 --> 00:22:40.619
NYPD! Do not move!

538
00:22:40.620 --> 00:22:42.664
- Warrant.
- What the hell?

539
00:22:42.665 --> 00:22:44.666
Keep him there.

540
00:22:44.667 --> 00:22:51.848
<i>♪</i>

541
00:22:58.551 --> 00:22:59.813
Crowbar.

542
00:23:16.264 --> 00:23:17.439
[tapping]

543
00:23:31.497 --> 00:23:33.107
Uh-huh.

544
00:23:34.195 --> 00:23:37.066
Looky here. Rolex
with a blue face.

545
00:23:37.067 --> 00:23:38.894
Turn around and put your
hands behind your back.

546
00:23:38.895 --> 00:23:40.287
What are you talking about?

547
00:23:40.288 --> 00:23:43.029
We found a unique and
expensive timepiece

548
00:23:43.030 --> 00:23:44.813
in your desk.
- What the hell does that mean?

549
00:23:44.814 --> 00:23:47.425
It means you're under arrest.

550
00:23:47.426 --> 00:23:49.992
We have the former
player's testimony.

551
00:23:49.993 --> 00:23:51.994
the watch. and
surveillance footage

552
00:23:51.995 --> 00:23:54.040
of Costa two blocks
from the crime scene

553
00:23:54.041 --> 00:23:55.694
a few minutes
after the 911 call.

554
00:23:55.695 --> 00:23:58.261
- What about the murder weapon?
- Police never recovered it.

555
00:23:58.262 --> 00:24:01.308
- Motive?
- I'm not sure.

556
00:24:01.309 --> 00:24:02.831
At the moment. we're
assuming it's something to do

557
00:24:02.832 --> 00:24:04.659
with the former player's debt.

558
00:24:04.660 --> 00:24:06.487
Sounds like Walsh was meeting up

559
00:24:06.488 --> 00:24:07.923
with Costa to pay it off.

560
00:24:07.924 --> 00:24:10.404
Why kill someone who's
giving you money?

561
00:24:10.405 --> 00:24:12.101
It doesn't make sense.
- I know.

562
00:24:12.102 --> 00:24:13.668
We'll keep digging.

563
00:24:13.669 --> 00:24:16.366
[phone buzzing]

564
00:24:16.367 --> 00:24:18.151
Jalen.

565
00:24:18.152 --> 00:24:20.153
Look. I found the
gun in the trash.

566
00:24:20.154 --> 00:24:22.634
I didn't shoot nobody. I swear.

567
00:24:22.635 --> 00:24:24.374
I saw some dude toss it.

568
00:24:24.375 --> 00:24:27.508
You saw someone throw the
gun into the dumpster?

569
00:24:27.509 --> 00:24:29.771
Yeah. a white dude.

570
00:24:29.772 --> 00:24:35.255
Can you describe him.
age. height. body type?

571
00:24:35.256 --> 00:24:36.517
Nah.

572
00:24:36.518 --> 00:24:38.214
So you've just
been walking around

573
00:24:38.215 --> 00:24:39.825
with that gun for three days?

574
00:24:39.826 --> 00:24:42.175
Yeah. but I never shot it.

575
00:24:42.176 --> 00:24:43.785
I just thought it'd
be cool. you know?

576
00:24:43.786 --> 00:24:45.221
No. I don't know.

577
00:24:45.222 --> 00:24:48.182
Because it's not cool to
walk around with a gun.

578
00:24:51.011 --> 00:24:52.229
You hear what I said?

579
00:24:53.970 --> 00:24:57.364
Yeah. I heard you.

580
00:24:57.365 --> 00:25:02.065
You remember where you found
the gun. exact location?

581
00:25:05.808 --> 00:25:07.505
This is Costa.

582
00:25:07.506 --> 00:25:09.376
approximately 100
yards from the dumpster

583
00:25:09.377 --> 00:25:11.378
where the young
man found the gun.

584
00:25:11.379 --> 00:25:13.293
- How close to the crime scene?
- Three blocks.

585
00:25:13.294 --> 00:25:15.338
And the timestamp on the
video is helpful as well.

586
00:25:15.339 --> 00:25:17.166
five minutes after the 911 call.

587
00:25:17.167 --> 00:25:18.472
And we're sure that's
the murder weapon?

588
00:25:18.473 --> 00:25:19.821
Ballistics report just came in.

589
00:25:19.822 --> 00:25:21.301
Okay. good.

590
00:25:21.302 --> 00:25:22.607
So we can tie Costa
to the murder weapon.

591
00:25:22.608 --> 00:25:24.130
Sort of.

592
00:25:24.131 --> 00:25:27.046
It's not ideal.
but it is helpful.

593
00:25:27.047 --> 00:25:28.482
But still no motive.

594
00:25:28.483 --> 00:25:30.658
No. but the evidence is strong.

595
00:25:30.659 --> 00:25:33.269
It should be enough to
compensate for that.

596
00:25:33.270 --> 00:25:35.184
Okay. let's move forward.

597
00:25:35.185 --> 00:25:36.926
Charge him with murder two.

598
00:25:41.627 --> 00:25:44.498
We can tie the
defendant. Jack Costa.

599
00:25:44.499 --> 00:25:48.415
to both the murder weapon
and the crime scene.

600
00:25:48.416 --> 00:25:52.201
We can also tie him to
the victim. Nick Walsh.

601
00:25:52.202 --> 00:25:56.902
and prove he had access to
him on the day of the murder.

602
00:25:56.903 --> 00:26:01.210
No. we don't have an
eyewitness who saw him

603
00:26:01.211 --> 00:26:04.605
shoot Nick Walsh or
video showing him

604
00:26:04.606 --> 00:26:09.567
fleeing the crime. gun in hand.
but the evidence we do have

605
00:26:09.568 --> 00:26:13.309
paints a compelling picture
of what happened that day.

606
00:26:13.310 --> 00:26:18.184
and it will prove beyond
a reasonable doubt

607
00:26:18.185 --> 00:26:23.016
that the defendant
murdered Nick Walsh.

608
00:26:27.629 --> 00:26:30.762
Let me translate what
Mr. Price just said.

609
00:26:30.763 --> 00:26:33.068
We have a lousy case.

610
00:26:33.069 --> 00:26:37.638
and we aren't really sure that
Jack Costa committed the crime.

611
00:26:37.639 --> 00:26:43.601
Nick Walsh was an
animated and fiery coach

612
00:26:43.602 --> 00:26:48.562
with lots of notoriety
and lots of enemies.

613
00:26:48.563 --> 00:26:51.826
He was a hometown hero
who helped lead Hudson

614
00:26:51.827 --> 00:26:54.350
to unprecedented success.

615
00:26:54.351 --> 00:26:58.659
but he was on the
verge of leaving.

616
00:26:58.660 --> 00:27:04.056
chasing bigger. better.
shinier dreams at a new school.

617
00:27:04.057 --> 00:27:06.493
He was in the middle of
negotiating a contract

618
00:27:06.494 --> 00:27:11.106
that would be worth
over $100 million.

619
00:27:11.107 --> 00:27:13.369
The fans were upset.

620
00:27:13.370 --> 00:27:15.241
They thought he was disloyal.

621
00:27:15.242 --> 00:27:18.724
They accused him of using
Hudson as a stepping stone.

622
00:27:20.639 --> 00:27:23.684
Like it or not.
there were thousands

623
00:27:23.685 --> 00:27:26.339
of irrational and
disgruntled fans

624
00:27:26.340 --> 00:27:30.212
who thought Nick
Walsh was a traitor.

625
00:27:30.213 --> 00:27:33.651
and any one of them could
have pulled that trigger.

626
00:27:33.652 --> 00:27:36.305
including the teenage boy

627
00:27:36.306 --> 00:27:41.093
who just so happens to
find the murder weapon

628
00:27:41.094 --> 00:27:44.705
and who just so happens
to be a die-hard

629
00:27:44.706 --> 00:27:47.360
Hudson U Basketball fan.

630
00:27:47.361 --> 00:27:51.191
Bottom line. there's
no motive here.

631
00:27:53.541 --> 00:27:58.545
Jack Costa is a
hardworking businessman

632
00:27:58.546 --> 00:28:03.245
who never met Nick Walsh.
so he had absolutely

633
00:28:03.246 --> 00:28:06.293
no reason to kill him.

634
00:28:08.338 --> 00:28:10.252
Did your husband own a watch?

635
00:28:10.253 --> 00:28:13.125
- Yes.
- Can you describe it?

636
00:28:13.126 --> 00:28:17.912
It was a Rolex. blue
face. white markers.

637
00:28:17.913 --> 00:28:22.525
and a platinum-and-gold band.

638
00:28:22.526 --> 00:28:27.617
Does this watch look like
the one your husband owned?

639
00:28:27.618 --> 00:28:29.532
Yes. definitely.

640
00:28:29.533 --> 00:28:31.404
That's it.

641
00:28:31.405 --> 00:28:34.146
Let the record reflect
the watch Mrs. Walsh

642
00:28:34.147 --> 00:28:37.236
just identified was
the watch recovered

643
00:28:37.237 --> 00:28:39.586
from the defendant's office.

644
00:28:39.587 --> 00:28:42.372
- So noted.
- Nothing further.

645
00:28:44.026 --> 00:28:46.767
Your husband's watch
wasn't registered. correct?

646
00:28:46.768 --> 00:28:49.639
So there's no way of proving
that that's the same watch.

647
00:28:49.640 --> 00:28:51.076
I'm not sure.

648
00:28:51.077 --> 00:28:53.382
One of Nick's former players
gave it to him the day

649
00:28:53.383 --> 00:28:54.862
after he signed a new contract.

650
00:28:54.863 --> 00:28:58.126
That may be true.
but you don't know

651
00:28:58.127 --> 00:29:00.346
that that's the same watch.

652
00:29:00.347 --> 00:29:02.914
No. that's the watch.

653
00:29:02.915 --> 00:29:05.264
Nick wore it every day.

654
00:29:05.265 --> 00:29:08.615
He said it reminded him
what his job really was.

655
00:29:08.616 --> 00:29:11.749
to help kids achieve
their dreams.

656
00:29:11.750 --> 00:29:13.620
The crime lab tested the watch

657
00:29:13.621 --> 00:29:15.448
that the police found
in my client's bar

658
00:29:15.449 --> 00:29:17.972
for your husband's DNA.

659
00:29:17.973 --> 00:29:20.193
The test came back negative.

660
00:29:21.672 --> 00:29:22.803
I didn't know.

661
00:29:22.804 --> 00:29:24.936
One more thing you
probably didn't know.

662
00:29:24.937 --> 00:29:27.982
the watch you just looked
at. the Submariner.

663
00:29:27.983 --> 00:29:29.636
it's a very popular watch.

664
00:29:29.637 --> 00:29:32.247
There's literally thousands
of them in existence.

665
00:29:32.248 --> 00:29:35.598
the same brand.
model. face. color.

666
00:29:35.599 --> 00:29:40.038
The manufacturer released
1.200 of them just this year.

667
00:29:40.039 --> 00:29:42.127
So there's no way of determining

668
00:29:42.128 --> 00:29:44.216
that the watch
you just looked at

669
00:29:44.217 --> 00:29:47.436
actually belonged
to your husband.

670
00:29:47.437 --> 00:29:51.136
<i>[tense music]</i>

671
00:29:51.137 --> 00:29:54.488
I... I suppose you're right.

672
00:29:58.884 --> 00:30:00.536
I know. Sam. we're looking.
but I'm telling you.

673
00:30:00.537 --> 00:30:01.973
there's nothing else to move on.

674
00:30:01.974 --> 00:30:03.322
I get it.

675
00:30:03.323 --> 00:30:05.541
Problem is. the defense
is picking us apart.

676
00:30:05.542 --> 00:30:08.370
so we need something
else. something new.

677
00:30:08.371 --> 00:30:10.068
preferably something
that explains

678
00:30:10.069 --> 00:30:11.983
why Costa actually killed Walsh.

679
00:30:11.984 --> 00:30:14.681
Look. we have zero evidence
that points to motive.

680
00:30:14.682 --> 00:30:17.640
And trust me. Costa's friends.
they're not cooperating.

681
00:30:17.641 --> 00:30:21.557
These guys eat. drink. and
sleep this omertà nonsense.

682
00:30:21.558 --> 00:30:24.734
Someone in that crowd has
to have a shred of humanity

683
00:30:24.735 --> 00:30:27.868
and realize that when a
person kills an innocent man.

684
00:30:27.869 --> 00:30:29.304
he has to pay.

685
00:30:29.305 --> 00:30:31.220
I'm not so sure about that.

686
00:30:36.312 --> 00:30:37.878
Sorry. Vin.

687
00:30:37.879 --> 00:30:41.186
All the beer in my fridge
actually has alcohol in it.

688
00:30:41.187 --> 00:30:43.188
Maybe it shouldn't.

689
00:30:43.189 --> 00:30:46.801
Come on. don't start with all
that "bad genes" crap again.

690
00:30:48.455 --> 00:30:53.198
Listen. Matt. you need
to tell me what you know.

691
00:30:53.199 --> 00:30:55.374
all right? What
you really know.

692
00:30:55.375 --> 00:30:57.942
And you need to
tell me right now.

693
00:30:57.943 --> 00:31:01.293
Mm-hmm. yeah. I already did.

694
00:31:01.294 --> 00:31:03.382
Did he confess?

695
00:31:03.383 --> 00:31:04.731
Did he say that he shot Walsh?

696
00:31:04.732 --> 00:31:06.472
I don't wanna get
involved. all right?

697
00:31:06.473 --> 00:31:08.387
It's not my job.
- God. what... [stammers]

698
00:31:08.388 --> 00:31:10.476
What is wrong with you. huh?

699
00:31:10.477 --> 00:31:11.781
Walsh had a wife. He
had two little girls.

700
00:31:11.782 --> 00:31:13.131
And you don't care
that your friend

701
00:31:13.132 --> 00:31:15.350
put two bullets in his chest?

702
00:31:15.351 --> 00:31:18.049
Of course. I care.

703
00:31:18.050 --> 00:31:20.529
Matt. if you know something.
this is the only way

704
00:31:20.530 --> 00:31:22.227
to get rid of the gun charge.
- Oh. please.

705
00:31:22.228 --> 00:31:24.229
There's gotta be 100 ways to
make the gun charge go away.

706
00:31:24.230 --> 00:31:27.362
There's not. There's one.

707
00:31:27.363 --> 00:31:29.408
And this is it.

708
00:31:29.409 --> 00:31:32.411
I can't do it. I'm
not that kind of guy.

709
00:31:32.412 --> 00:31:34.413
You're not that kind of guy?

710
00:31:34.414 --> 00:31:35.980
The kind of guy that
thinks that murderers

711
00:31:35.981 --> 00:31:38.852
should actually go to prison?

712
00:31:38.853 --> 00:31:41.115
You're my brother.

713
00:31:41.116 --> 00:31:43.596
but we're different.

714
00:31:43.597 --> 00:31:46.468
I look out for my
friends. no matter what.

715
00:31:46.469 --> 00:31:49.776
Are you listening to
yourself right now. huh?

716
00:31:49.777 --> 00:31:52.735
You actually believe this crap?

717
00:31:52.736 --> 00:31:54.085
Let me tell you something.

718
00:31:54.086 --> 00:31:56.087
This is not some Scorsese movie

719
00:31:56.088 --> 00:31:58.089
where you and your friends
kick it around the neighborhood

720
00:31:58.090 --> 00:32:01.614
spouting off all this tough
guy talk with no consequences.

721
00:32:01.615 --> 00:32:02.963
This is real.

722
00:32:02.964 --> 00:32:05.009
And you need to look out
for yourself right now.

723
00:32:05.010 --> 00:32:06.662
You understand me?

724
00:32:06.663 --> 00:32:09.362
Not some punk named Costa
who doesn't care about you.

725
00:32:11.016 --> 00:32:12.451
This is the moment. Matt.

726
00:32:12.452 --> 00:32:14.366
This is your moment.

727
00:32:14.367 --> 00:32:16.498
and this is your last chance.

728
00:32:16.499 --> 00:32:23.680
<i>♪</i>

729
00:32:29.991 --> 00:32:32.253
Costa said that Walsh
was a good guy. you know.

730
00:32:32.254 --> 00:32:33.472
and that he cared
about his players.

731
00:32:33.473 --> 00:32:36.910
and so he thought he
had him over a barrel.

732
00:32:36.911 --> 00:32:38.564
Meaning what?

733
00:32:38.565 --> 00:32:40.261
Thought he could jam him up.

734
00:32:40.262 --> 00:32:42.785
You know. ask for more
money than the kid owed.

735
00:32:42.786 --> 00:32:45.223
Uh-huh. Can you
be more specific?

736
00:32:45.224 --> 00:32:47.834
Kid owed. like.
75 grand. I think.

737
00:32:47.835 --> 00:32:50.968
Costa was gonna ask for...
I don't know... 150.

738
00:32:50.969 --> 00:32:52.927
[chuckles]

739
00:32:54.711 --> 00:32:57.104
What else did he tell you?

740
00:32:57.105 --> 00:33:02.457
That when he asked Walsh.
he got upset. you know?

741
00:33:02.458 --> 00:33:04.372
Real upset.

742
00:33:04.373 --> 00:33:06.809
<i>[pensive music]</i>

743
00:33:06.810 --> 00:33:09.335
Things got out of hand.

744
00:33:14.209 --> 00:33:16.472
Did Costa confess
to shooting him?

745
00:33:21.521 --> 00:33:26.004
Like I said. Walsh got angry.
threatened to kick his ass.

746
00:33:27.875 --> 00:33:29.963
Costa did what he had to do.

747
00:33:29.964 --> 00:33:32.184
Those your words or his?

748
00:33:34.447 --> 00:33:36.188
His.

749
00:33:40.975 --> 00:33:42.323
Yeah.

750
00:33:42.324 --> 00:33:44.630
When we're in court.
answer the questions

751
00:33:44.631 --> 00:33:47.590
like you did just now.

752
00:33:53.944 --> 00:33:56.381
You're doing the
right thing. Matt.

753
00:33:56.382 --> 00:34:02.691
<i>♪</i>

754
00:34:02.692 --> 00:34:05.651
Did you and the defendant
ever discuss the circumstances

755
00:34:05.652 --> 00:34:07.305
of Nick Walsh's murder?

756
00:34:07.306 --> 00:34:08.784
Yeah.

757
00:34:08.785 --> 00:34:09.959
Did he tell you
why he was meeting

758
00:34:09.960 --> 00:34:11.787
Mr. Walsh that afternoon?

759
00:34:11.788 --> 00:34:15.052
Yeah. he said. uh...

760
00:34:15.053 --> 00:34:17.054
said Walsh was gonna
pay off the debt

761
00:34:17.055 --> 00:34:19.752
of one of his former players.

762
00:34:19.753 --> 00:34:21.407
He say anything else?

763
00:34:26.629 --> 00:34:27.629
No. not really.

764
00:34:31.547 --> 00:34:35.028
Did he mention any
other reason for meeting

765
00:34:35.029 --> 00:34:38.031
Mr. Walsh that day?

766
00:34:38.032 --> 00:34:41.730
Was he planning to
discuss or demand

767
00:34:41.731 --> 00:34:43.906
anything else from Mr. Walsh?

768
00:34:43.907 --> 00:34:48.128
<i>[tense music]</i>

769
00:34:48.129 --> 00:34:52.393
Mr. Riley. did the
defendant tell you

770
00:34:52.394 --> 00:34:53.960
what he planned
to ask Mr. Walsh

771
00:34:53.961 --> 00:34:55.962
when they met up in person?

772
00:34:55.963 --> 00:34:58.573
No.

773
00:34:58.574 --> 00:35:02.970
Never... never told you what
they planned to discuss?

774
00:35:04.798 --> 00:35:06.365
No.

775
00:35:09.716 --> 00:35:12.892
Did the defendant ever tell
you who shot Mr. Walsh?

776
00:35:12.893 --> 00:35:14.154
No.

777
00:35:14.155 --> 00:35:16.462
I'd like to request
a brief recess.

778
00:35:20.118 --> 00:35:21.422
What's going on?

779
00:35:21.423 --> 00:35:23.120
You said you were
willing to testify.

780
00:35:23.121 --> 00:35:25.644
I guess I changed my mind.

781
00:35:25.645 --> 00:35:28.169
Are you serious?

782
00:35:29.997 --> 00:35:31.693
Guess so.

783
00:35:31.694 --> 00:35:38.658
<i>♪</i>

784
00:35:41.051 --> 00:35:44.793
What the hell is
the matter with you?

785
00:35:44.794 --> 00:35:46.708
This is a murder trial. Matt.

786
00:35:46.709 --> 00:35:48.057
You understand that?
You're under oath.

787
00:35:48.058 --> 00:35:49.276
Yeah. I know.

788
00:35:49.277 --> 00:35:52.410
I thought I could do
it. Vin. but. uh...

789
00:35:52.411 --> 00:35:55.501
[chuckles] I can't do it.

790
00:35:57.329 --> 00:35:59.418
You know that this
is your last...

791
00:36:12.082 --> 00:36:13.474
Your Honor. the
witness's answers

792
00:36:13.475 --> 00:36:15.346
are inconsistent with
his previous statements.

793
00:36:15.347 --> 00:36:17.304
As such. I'd like to treat
him as a hostile witness.

794
00:36:17.305 --> 00:36:19.351
Yes. I'll allow it.

795
00:36:21.701 --> 00:36:26.270
Mr. Riley. you presented
a sworn affidavit

796
00:36:26.271 --> 00:36:28.359
to me stating that the defendant

797
00:36:28.360 --> 00:36:30.926
planned to exploit
Mr. Walsh's compassion

798
00:36:30.927 --> 00:36:32.101
for his former player.

799
00:36:32.102 --> 00:36:33.494
Objection. Hearsay.

800
00:36:33.495 --> 00:36:34.930
Your Honor. it was
a sworn statement.

801
00:36:34.931 --> 00:36:37.194
I'm offering it for
impeachment purposes only.

802
00:36:37.195 --> 00:36:39.631
Okay. but that's
as far as it goes.

803
00:36:39.632 --> 00:36:40.893
Overruled.

804
00:36:40.894 --> 00:36:43.504
The defendant's plan
was to ask Mr. Walsh

805
00:36:43.505 --> 00:36:45.376
for double the amount
Jordan Crawford

806
00:36:45.377 --> 00:36:47.204
actually owed. correct?

807
00:36:47.205 --> 00:36:48.596
I don't know
anything about that.

808
00:36:48.597 --> 00:36:50.511
And because of this.
the two men fought.

809
00:36:50.512 --> 00:36:51.947
Objection.

810
00:36:51.948 --> 00:36:53.949
This is being offered as
the truth. not impeachment.

811
00:36:53.950 --> 00:36:55.516
Sustained.

812
00:36:55.517 --> 00:36:58.911
Mr. Price. for
impeachment purposes only.

813
00:36:58.912 --> 00:37:01.262
I won't ask again.

814
00:37:06.136 --> 00:37:09.574
Your refusal to
cooperate here today.

815
00:37:09.575 --> 00:37:14.231
to not answer my questions
in a truthful manner

816
00:37:14.232 --> 00:37:17.364
is based on your desire
to help the defendant?

817
00:37:17.365 --> 00:37:19.018
I'm just telling
you what I know.

818
00:37:19.019 --> 00:37:23.805
You think it's a cowardly act
to testify against a friend.

819
00:37:23.806 --> 00:37:25.546
regardless of his
guilt or innocence.

820
00:37:25.547 --> 00:37:26.808
Isn't that true?

821
00:37:26.809 --> 00:37:28.984
That snitching is a
crime unto itself.

822
00:37:28.985 --> 00:37:32.379
that ratting someone out is
an unforgivable betrayal.

823
00:37:32.380 --> 00:37:34.425
I don't know what your point is.

824
00:37:34.426 --> 00:37:39.168
My point is that you
agreed to tell the truth.

825
00:37:39.169 --> 00:37:40.648
but you didn't do it.

826
00:37:40.649 --> 00:37:43.042
You couldn't do it.
because in your mind.

827
00:37:43.043 --> 00:37:45.087
it's better to let
a killer go free

828
00:37:45.088 --> 00:37:49.570
than testify against a friend.

829
00:37:49.571 --> 00:37:51.050
Am I right? Is
that how you think?

830
00:37:51.051 --> 00:37:53.661
Better to be a stand-up guy
and keep your mouth shut.

831
00:37:53.662 --> 00:37:55.272
Yeah. You're damn right it is.

832
00:37:55.273 --> 00:37:56.577
Even if the consequence
of that silence

833
00:37:56.578 --> 00:37:59.363
is to let a killer walk free?

834
00:37:59.364 --> 00:38:01.714
That doesn't bother you?

835
00:38:03.716 --> 00:38:05.282
Not in the least.

836
00:38:05.283 --> 00:38:12.420
<i>♪</i>

837
00:38:13.987 --> 00:38:15.815
Nothing further.

838
00:38:17.817 --> 00:38:20.253
Ms. Gallo?

839
00:38:20.254 --> 00:38:21.994
No questions.

840
00:38:21.995 --> 00:38:29.176
<i>♪</i>

841
00:38:39.708 --> 00:38:41.493
Please rise.

842
00:38:46.802 --> 00:38:49.108
In the matter of
People versus Costa.

843
00:38:49.109 --> 00:38:51.153
has the jury reached a verdict?

844
00:38:51.154 --> 00:38:52.764
Yes. we have. Your Honor.

845
00:38:52.765 --> 00:38:54.505
How do you find?

846
00:38:54.506 --> 00:38:57.509
We find the defendant guilty.

847
00:39:01.730 --> 00:39:05.951
Members of the jury. I'd like
to thank you for your service.

848
00:39:05.952 --> 00:39:08.127
Court is adjourned.

849
00:39:08.128 --> 00:39:09.258
[gavel bangs]

850
00:39:09.259 --> 00:39:16.354
<i>♪</i>

851
00:39:20.706 --> 00:39:22.750
Guess it all worked out. huh?

852
00:39:22.751 --> 00:39:24.883
Yeah.

853
00:39:24.884 --> 00:39:26.493
Just happy for the
Walsh family. man.

854
00:39:26.494 --> 00:39:28.365
They really needed the W.

855
00:39:28.366 --> 00:39:29.715
Yeah. so did you.

856
00:39:33.588 --> 00:39:36.198
You know. Vince.
you're a great cop.

857
00:39:36.199 --> 00:39:39.376
People really respect you.

858
00:39:39.377 --> 00:39:41.769
But if Costa had
been acquitted...

859
00:39:41.770 --> 00:39:48.734
<i>♪</i>

860
00:39:53.913 --> 00:39:56.305
[knocking]

861
00:39:56.306 --> 00:39:58.613
Matty. it's Vince.

862
00:40:03.270 --> 00:40:06.185
<i>[pop music playing]</i>

863
00:40:06.186 --> 00:40:09.667
<i>♪</i>

864
00:40:09.668 --> 00:40:13.322
Yeah. I'll be right back.

865
00:40:13.323 --> 00:40:15.499
[chuckles] What are you doing?

866
00:40:15.500 --> 00:40:17.065
You know. I wish you'd called.

867
00:40:17.066 --> 00:40:20.940
I. uh. I got a lady
friend over. you know?

868
00:40:22.942 --> 00:40:24.377
You and your ladies.

869
00:40:24.378 --> 00:40:26.418
Yeah. well. at least I'm
good at something. right?

870
00:40:31.341 --> 00:40:33.081
Listen. we gotta take a ride.

871
00:40:33.082 --> 00:40:35.780
All right. Where?

872
00:40:35.781 --> 00:40:39.131
The precinct.

873
00:40:39.132 --> 00:40:40.393
What are you talking about?

874
00:40:40.394 --> 00:40:43.222
The gun case.

875
00:40:43.223 --> 00:40:44.876
They're gonna charge you.

876
00:40:44.877 --> 00:40:46.443
Get out of here. What
are you talking...

877
00:40:46.444 --> 00:40:47.792
you said you were
gonna make a call.

878
00:40:47.793 --> 00:40:49.010
make it go away.

879
00:40:49.011 --> 00:40:51.883
Yeah. well. I guess
I changed my mind.

880
00:40:51.884 --> 00:40:54.755
<i>[tense music]</i>

881
00:40:54.756 --> 00:40:56.670
Look. Vin. I'm sorry. all right?

882
00:40:56.671 --> 00:40:58.411
But you gotta help me out.

883
00:40:58.412 --> 00:40:59.934
You gotta give me
another chance here.

884
00:40:59.935 --> 00:41:01.501
I'll come through.
- I can't do it anymore. Matt.

885
00:41:01.502 --> 00:41:04.331
- I promise.
- I can't do it.

886
00:41:10.859 --> 00:41:13.340
Come on. let's go.

887
00:41:19.172 --> 00:41:20.302
Come on.

888
00:41:20.303 --> 00:41:27.485
<i>♪</i>

889
00:41:41.194 --> 00:41:44.152
<i>[dramatic music]</i>

890
00:41:44.153 --> 00:41:51.378
<i>♪</i>

891
00:42:11.224 --> 00:42:14.140
[wolf howls]

892
